1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,625
For one harvest season,

2
00:00:01,625 --> 00:00:04,512
it looked like the famine problem was solved.

3
00:00:04,512 --> 00:00:07,655
Then, in the summer of 1914, Europe went to war —

4
00:00:07,655 --> 00:00:12,210
and Britain's navy cut off Germany's imported nitrate supply overnight.

5
00:00:12,210 --> 00:00:15,867
Germany needed nitrogen for one more purpose: explosives.

6
00:00:15,867 --> 00:00:20,036
The same Haber-Bosch process built to grow food was reengineered,

7
00:00:20,036 --> 00:00:24,270
almost immediately, to manufacture the raw material for munitions.

8
00:00:24,270 --> 00:00:29,146
Historians still debate exactly how much this one factory extended Germany's

9
00:00:29,146 --> 00:00:30,813
ability to keep fighting —

10
00:00:30,813 --> 00:00:33,828
the evidence doesn't support a precise number —

11
00:00:33,828 --> 00:00:37,421
but the war would have looked very different without it.

